<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S3.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Bias detection using prompting (zero-shot or in-context) and fine-tuning (default <span id="S3.T3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">unw.</span> or reweighted <span id="S3.T3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">rew.</span> prediction loss). Binary indicates unbiased (negative) vs biased (positive) detection. Other measures are for multi-label bias prediction of bias targets. For MR and <math id="S3.T3.m194" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> scores, higher is better; for HL, FPR, and FNR, lower is better. Time: median inference time in milliseconds.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
